# TRANSITIONAL. Delete this file.
#
# It exists only because the work tree is $HOME, so every path Arch or an
# application creates there has to be denied by name. The enumerated list is
# deliberate: an entry that is not listed shows up in `git status`, which is
# how a new dotfile gets noticed.
#
# That stops being useful once every dotfile is a home-manager module, because
# then the answer for anything new in $HOME is never "track it" but "write a
# module". At that point the repo moves to a normal project directory, home
# manager writes into $HOME, and this file goes away rather than shrinking.
#
# Until Arch is gone, it stays.

